From: OpenHarmony Compiler <ohc@opendesk.org>
Date: 2026-06-04
Subject: Disable CMake build system to force meson detection

peek has both CMakeLists.txt and meson.build files. The ohc-run.py
build driver detects cmake first when CMakeLists.txt exists, but
cmake fails on OpenHarmony. The primary build system for peek is
meson, so we rename CMakeLists.txt to CMakeLists.txt.disabled to
force meson detection.

This patch renames all CMakeLists.txt files to .disabled suffix.
No actual source code changes are made.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt.disabled
similarity index 100%
rename from CMakeLists.txt
rename to CMakeLists.txt.disabled

diff --git a/data/CMakeLists.txt b/data/CMakeLists.txt.disabled
similarity index 100%
rename from data/CMakeLists.txt
rename to data/CMakeLists.txt.disabled

diff --git a/data/man/CMakeLists.txt b/data/man/CMakeLists.txt.disabled
similarity index 100%
rename from data/man/CMakeLists.txt
rename to data/man/CMakeLists.txt.disabled

diff --git a/po/CMakeLists.txt b/po/CMakeLists.txt.disabled
similarity index 100%
rename from po/CMakeLists.txt
rename to po/CMakeLists.txt.disabled

diff --git a/tests/CMakeLists.txt b/tests/CMakeLists.txt.disabled
similarity index 100%
rename from tests/CMakeLists.txt
rename to tests/CMakeLists.txt.disabled
